**Diagram 2: Abstracted High-Level Cloud Container Architecture Overview**

This diagram generalizes the two main patterns you used (Serverless Container Platform like Cloud Run/App Runner and Managed VM like GCE/EC2) for the combined container approach.

```plantuml
@startuml Abstract Cloud Container Deployment (Combined Container)

title Abstracted Cloud Container Deployment Patterns (Combined App)

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam node {
    borderColor Black
    borderThickness 1
}
skinparam component {
    borderColor Black
    borderThickness 1
}
skinparam rectangle {
    borderColor Black
    borderThickness 1
}

actor "User / Client" as User

package "Cloud Provider (AWS / GCP)" {

    rectangle "Pattern 1: Serverless Container Platform\n(e.g., Cloud Run, App Runner)" as ServerlessPattern {
        node "Managed Service Instance" as ServerlessInstance {
           interface "Public HTTPS URL" as ServerlessURL
           node "Container Instance (Ephemeral)" as ServerlessContainer {
               component "App Process\n(Listens 8080)" as ServerlessApp
               component "DB Process\n(Listens 5432)" as ServerlessDB
           }
        }
        ServerlessApp -> ServerlessDB : localhost:5432
    }

    rectangle "Pattern 2: Managed VM + Docker\n(e.g., EC2, Compute Engine)" as VMPattern {
       node "VM Instance" as VM {
          interface "External IP Address:8080" as VMIP
           node "OS + Docker Engine" as VMDocker {
                node "Docker Volume\n(Persistent)" as VMVol
                node "Running Container" as VMContainer {
                    component "App Process\n(Listens 8080)" as VMApp
                    component "DB Process\n(Listens 5432)" as VMDB
                }
           }
       }
       VMApp -> VMDB : localhost:5432
       VMDB ..> VMVol : R/W Data
    }

    package "Cloud Networking & Security (Conceptual)" {
        node "Firewall / Security Group" as Firewall
        node "VPC / Network" as VPC
        node "Load Balancer / Gateway (Implied)" as LB
    }

}

' --- Simplified Flows ---
User --> ServerlessURL : Request (HTTPS)
User --> VMIP : Request (HTTP:8080)

ServerlessURL --> ServerlessInstance : Managed Routing
VMIP --> VM : Network Routing (via Firewall)
VM --> VMDocker : OS/Docker Port Mapping
VMDocker --> VMContainer : Delivers Request


@enduml